 short-term investment of the Rs 4.3bn rights-issue proceeds raised in the March 2026 quarter, partially offset by a much smaller share-of-profit contribution from equity-accounted investees (Rs 45.1mn vs Rs 136.9mn a year earlier, when a one-off Rs 1.27bn gain from an associate-to-subsidiary reclassification inflated that line). The company completed a 2-for-1 rights issue in the prior quarter, raising Rs 4.3bn and tripling shares in issue from 307.1mn to 921.2mn; public shareholding fell correspondingly from 49.96% to 27.25%.", "source_doc_id": "52079", "source_page": 1, "gaps_note": "Revenue is structurally nil/minimal -- an investment holding company business-model characteristic, not a data gap. cost_of_sales/gross_profit are not applicable and left blank.", "takeaway": "Ceylon Land & Equity's profit continued to grow (Group PAT up 17.7% year-on-year) after a transformative March-2026 quarter that saw a 2-for-1 rights issue triple its share count -- but the company remains structurally revenue-light, an investment-holding profile, not an operating gap.", "qoq": [{"metric": "revenue", "label": "Revenue", "prior_period_label": "Quarter ended 31 March 2026", "prior_value": 353.0, "new_period_label": "Quarter ended 30 June 2026", "new_value": 0.0, "pct_change": -1.0, "direction": "deteriorated", "prior_period_end_date": "2026-03-31", "new_period_end_date": "2026-06-30"}, {"metric": "operating_profit", "label": "Operating Profit", "prior_period_label": "Quarter ended 31 March 2026", "prior_value": 177412.0, "new_period_label": "Quarter ended 30 June 2026", "new_value": 71775.0, "pct_change": -0.5954332288683968, "direction": "deteriorated", "prior_period_end_date": "2026-03-31", "new_period_end_date": "2026-06-30"}, {"metric": "profit_before_tax", "label": "Profit Before Tax", "prior_period_label": "Quarter ended 31 March 2026", "prior_value": 149769.0, "new_period_label": "Quarter ended 30 June 2026", "new_value": 160393.0, "pct_change": 0.07093590796493267, "direc